      <floats-group id="article-19619.s16">
        <fig id="article-19619.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Clonorchis Life Cycle. The 3 species of adult flukes share a similar life cycle and differ slightly in size and in the arrangement of their testes and vitelline glands. Alexander J da Silva, PhD; Melanie Moser, Public Health Image Library, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://wwwn.cdc.gov/phil/Details.aspx?pid=3385">Public Domain</ext-link>, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</p>
